  "source_count": 12,
  "lines": 750,
  "scope": "An actual 44-slot counter/reversal machine derives every vertex label from the represented capacity-row cells, including empty input. Its returned list is consumed directly by the 8420-slot caller that allocates metadata and executes all parameter, initialization and iteration steps. The exact original solveInput state/event fields are returned with a same-run terminal-inclusive physical bound using only original n, demand count, capacity width and initial heap/address bounds. No vertex list, numeric labels or label-width certificate is supplied. Positive graph order, primitive capacity and adjacency-list representations, and demand records encoded by the internally generated label family remain premises. Initial primitive-list construction, outer degenerate dispatch and full-paper runtime remain separate."
}
